&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;iCapital is looking to hire an Associate Account Manager to support and grow relationships with an assigned portfolio of clients.This individual is responsible for account management and will be based remotely in the Midwest region.&amp;nbsp;This individual will play a key role in maintaining overall client health, driving platform adoption, supporting strategic initiatives, and ensuring clients maximize the value of iCapital&#39;s solutions through proactive engagement, training, and ongoing relationship management. This individual will serve as a trusted day-to-day partner to clients while collaborating closely with internal stakeholders to deliver a best-in-class client experience. This role will manage client relationships, coordinate resources across teams, identify opportunities for growth and expansion, and support the successful execution of strategic account plans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with assigned client accounts and serve as a primary point of contact for day-to-day client engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute account plans designed to improve client satisfaction, product utilization, relationship strength, retention, and overall account health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular client meetings, business reviews, and proactive outreach to maintain strong working relationships and understand evolving business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze client health, platform adoption, business objectives, and utilization trends to identify risks, opportunities, and actionable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted advisor by providing guidance on best practices, operational efficiencies, and strategic initiatives that support successful client outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead platform onboarding, implementation support, training, and adoption efforts to maximize client engagement and utilization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor account health and proactively identify risks, challenges, and opportunities for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support client retention and growth initiatives by identifying expansion opportunities and partnering with Sales and Strategic Account Management teams as appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and communicate on escalated client issues while partnering with Product, Client Delivery, Production Support, and other internal teams to drive successful resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track client priorities, strategic initiatives, enhancement requests, and action items to ensure visibility and progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the voice of the customer by communicating client feedback, business needs, operational challenges, and product enhancement opportunities internally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong collaborative relationships across Product, Client Delivery, Production Support, Finance, Sales, and Leadership teams to support client success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support renewal and commercial discussions through coordination, stakeholder management, follow-up activities, and internal alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present and demonstrate company products, capabilities, and solutions when appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate account plans, client activity records, and documentation within Salesforce and other approved systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep internal systems and records updated with relevant client notes, activities, and required information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in industry events, conferences, and client-facing activities to strengthen industry knowledge and professional networks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete ad hoc projects and assignments as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years of experience in account management, customer success, relationship management, client delivery, consulting, or other client-facing roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferred experience within financial services, insurance, InsureTech, FinTech, wealth management, or related industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage complex client relationships and multiple stakeholder groups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, presentation, relationship-building, and interpersonal skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong consultative problem-solving and client service orientation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and executing account plans and driving client engagement strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational, project management, and coordination capabilities with the ability to manage multiple priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to analyze client health, identify business needs, and develop actionable recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating across multiple departments and influencing outcomes without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and Salesforce or comparable CRM platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to work independently, proactively, and effectively in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel as needed for client meetings, business reviews, conferences, and team events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $70,000 to $80,000.&amp;nbsp; iCapital offers a compensation package which includes salary, equity for all full-time employees, and an annual performance bonus. Employees also receive a comprehensive benefits package that includes an employer matched retirement plan, generously subsidized healthcare with 100% employer paid dental, vision, telemedicine, and virtual mental health counseling, parental leave, and unlimited paid time off (PTO).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employees in this role will work fully remote based&amp;nbsp;in the Midwest region. Every department has different needs, and some positions will be designated in-office jobs, based on their function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For additional information on iCapital, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.icapitalnetwork.com/about-us&quot;&gt;https://www.icapitalnetwork.com/about-us&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;X: @icapitalnetwork | LinkedIn: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/icapital-network-inc&quot;&gt;https://www.linkedin.com/company/icapital-network-inc&lt;/a&gt; | Awards Disclaimer: &lt;a href=&quot;https://nam02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.icapitalnetwork.com%2Fabout-us%2Frecognition%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C01%7Ckturlis%40icapitalnetwork.com%7C7f07161790634b9fc3fc08da748bec16%7C0ac51d2823c34b35a9fbe1a17aa9eff1%7C0%7C0%7C637950441561507201%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=HAZm4uhhP8r6HVKnBqOMq5jbXmgOrHlsPCur9U4JRis%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;https://www.icapitalnetwork.com/about-us/recognition/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;iCapital is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This role supports the ongoing delivery of agentic AI–enabled automation across document-heavy and operational workflows. The intent is to move critical automation work off a high-cost contractor and into a lower-cost, full-time role without losing execution capability or momentum.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The focus is on building and supporting automation.&amp;nbsp; This is hands-on delivery work that is well understood, repeatable, and already embedded in core operational processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in building and enhancing agentic AI workflows that automate multi-step processes such as document intake, data extraction, validation, enrichment, and downstream routing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support integration of AI / ML and LLM-based models for document classification, entity extraction, and metadata generation, and connect those outputs into end-to-end automated workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain automation workflows and system integrations across document platforms, workflow engines, and operational systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with API integrations and data movement, ensuring secure, reliable flow between platforms with appropriate controls and auditability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support production automation by monitoring workflows, troubleshooting failures, addressing defects, and improving reliability through logging, retries, and validation checks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Product, Engineering, and Operations to translate known business requirements into implemented automation and to support ongoing enhancements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to documentation and standards so workflows are maintainable and not dependent on contractor knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in data science, machine learning or AI-related roles, with 3+ years leading cross-functional initiatives at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operationalizing AI/ML or advanced analytics solutions in production, ideally within financial services, fintech, or data-driven platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of LLMs, data science, AI/ML, and modern AI architectures, including model evaluation, context engineering, and agentic workflow automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and implementing agentic AI workflows, including multi-step AI agents that automate complex processes and integrate with enterprise systems, data, and APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or supporting production automation, ideally in document-heavy or regulated environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on exposure to AI-driven data extraction, document processing, or NLP-based workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with workflow orchestration, rules-based automation, and system integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working within established patterns and under technical direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execution-oriented, able to support existing platforms and improve them incrementally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe the best ideas and innovation happen when we are together. Employees in this role will work in the office four days, with the flexibility to work remotely one day (Friday). &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For additional information on iCapital Network, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.icapitalnetwork.com/about-us&quot;&gt;https://www.icapitalnetwork.com/about-us&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp; Twitter: @icapitalnetwork | LinkedIn: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/icapital-network-inc&quot;&gt;https://www.linkedin.com/company/icapital-network-inc&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;fortidlp-input-element-parent&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Artificial Intelligence Engineer - Vice President&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department: Software Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;iCapital is seeking a Vice President Artificial Intelligence Engineer to lead the design, development, and delivery of production-grade AI systems that drive measurable business outcomes across the firm. This individual will own key workstreams and serve as a technical leader, driving system design, mentoring engineers, partnering directly with business stakeholders, and ensuring that AI capabilities are built to production-grade standards of reliability, scalability, and measurability. The ideal candidate is a seasoned engineer with a track record of shipping complex AI systems end-to-end and someone who combines deep technical expertise with strong cross-functional partnership, architectural judgment, and able to operate as a force multiplier for the team. This role is expected to bring independent judgment on a technical approach, a bias toward delivery, and able to translate ambiguous business needs into well-scoped, well-executed solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the architecture and delivery of production AI systems, including document intelligence (IDP), intelligent knowledge systems, agentic orchestration, conversational AI, and generative AI applications, to power internal and external business processes, digital experiences, and workflow automation at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own AI projects end-to-end, from problem scoping and stakeholder alignment through solution design, implementation, deployment, monitoring, and continuous improvement, delivering tangible business outcomes with a track record of consistent, high-quality delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive technical design and architectural decisions for the team, including API design, system decomposition, evaluation strategy, and infrastructure patterns, establishing standards that raise the quality bar across the AI/ML platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and champion robust evaluation frameworks for AI systems, defining statistically sound, problem-specific metrics, curating benchmark datasets, and enforcing strict versioning to ensure reproducibility and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with cross-functional stakeholders, including the Product, Operations, Legal, and Business teams, to identify AI opportunities, translate requirements into technical plans, and communicate tradeoffs, risks, and recommendations clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and develop engineers on the team through code review, design review, pair problem-solving, and knowledge sharing, acting as a technical role model and raising the overall capability of the group.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify systemic problems and propose solutions, proactively improving team processes, tooling, and infrastructure to reduce technical debt and increase development velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience developing and deploying production AI/ML systems, including cloud-native solutions on AWS or similar platforms, with a proven track record of delivering complex applications from design through production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in Python and software engineering best practices, including source control, CI/CD, testing, documentation, and the development of scalable, maintainable software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise building production AI solutions, including LLM applications, AI agents, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), conversational AI, document intelligence, and agentic workflows, with hands-on experience using modern AI frameworks, tooling, and protocols such as MCP and A2A&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing, deploying, and operating end-to-end machine learning pipelines, including model training, deployment, monitoring, evaluation, and continuous improvement in production environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong foundation in statistics, experimentation, data quality, and AI system evaluation, with experience developing benchmarks, defining performance metrics, analyzing errors, and optimizing systems for accuracy, reliability, scalability, cost, and latency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading technical design and architectural decisions, conducting code and design reviews, mentoring engineers, and driving engineering excellence across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to document technical solutions, collaborate with cross-functional stakeholders, and communicate complex concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience spanning multiple AI domains, including LLM systems, document intelligence, and ML platforms or infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in financial services or FinTech, particularly within document-heavy, regulated, or compliance-sensitive environments is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributions to open-source projects, technical publications, conference presentations, patents, or other demonstrated thought leadership in applied AI and machine learning is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $170,000 to $210,000.&amp;nbsp; iCapital offers a compensation package which includes salary, equity for all full-time employees, and an annual performance bonus. Employees also receive a comprehensive benefits package that includes an employer matched retirement plan, generously subsidized healthcare with 100% employer paid dental, vision, telemedicine, and virtual mental health counseling, parental leave, and unlimited paid time off (PTO).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe the best ideas and innovation happen when we are together. Employees in this role will work in the office Monday-Thursday, with the flexibility to work remotely on Friday.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For additional information on iCapital, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://nam02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.icapitalnetwork.com%2Fabout-us&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7CRuth.Pyne%40icapital.com%7Cb434c603083746163dbd08df102d5dfd%7C0ac51d2823c34b35a9fbe1a17aa9eff1%7C0%7C0%7C639247459179560148%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=JVq7fW1nK6H9qPxJwLp4jL4W4n54Ft8a2nqtPUPSdRY%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;https://www.icapitalnetwork.com/about-us&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp; Twitter: @icapitalnetwork | LinkedIn: &lt;a href=&quot;https://nam02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Fcompany%2Ficapital-network-inc&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7CRuth.Pyne%40icapital.com%7Cb434c603083746163dbd08df102d5dfd%7C0ac51d2823c34b35a9fbe1a17aa9eff1%7C0%7C0%7C639247459179576831%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=gsgYp0lSxkdDKtWWaJKAvoAf8a4eGDBcT0axG%2FNUJjo%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;https://www.linkedin.com/company/icapital-network-inc&lt;/a&gt; | Awards Disclaimer: &lt;a href=&quot;https://nam02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.icapitalnetwork.com%2Fabout-us%2Frecognition%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C02%7CRuth.Pyne%40icapital.com%7Cb434c603083746163dbd08df102d5dfd%7C0ac51d2823c34b35a9fbe1a17aa9eff1%7C0%7C0%7C639247459179593695%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=gMISwxz5Z8fZdiisV7qYLYJA9vgt%2BJw0VNRtltpz%2FWY%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;https://www.icapitalnetwork.com/about-us/recognition/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;iCapital is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or other applicable legally protected characteristics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;fortidlp-input-element-parent&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;iCapital is seeking an Alternative Data Management Analyst to join the Data Solutions team. This individual must be comfortable working in a dynamic, performance-driven, fast-paced environment, and committed to delivering a high-quality, accurate product on a time-sensitive basis. The daily activities are diverse, from setting up and maintaining software applications, to ad hoc projects, and helping with data feed management. The role is a mix of finance and technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alternative Data Management
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Acquisition, Sourcing and Maintenance – manage source document and retrieval methods related to alternative investment products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Integrity – enrich unstructured data into existing data infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Quality and Controls – ensure completeness, timeliness and accuracy of relevant investment data through validation and control processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Governance – adhere to data governance best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration – collaborate across teams to provide insights from alternative investment data across multiple reporting platforms and systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation and Process improvement – continuously look for ways to automate and improve existing processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Documentation and Knowledge Sharing – maintain and share standard operating procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s in finance, Economics, Business Administration or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0 – 3 years in data management, analysis, or financial operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in data management tools, excel and other software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;General understanding of the alternative investment landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize and execute tasks and meet deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to continuously learn new technologies and adapt to new data and systems as industry evolves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify and understand risks associated with data management processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to support the team and build relationships across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $60,000 to $65,000.&amp;nbsp;This position is paid on an hourly basis and is classified as non-exempt. Employees in this role are eligible for overtime pay in accordance with applicable law. iCapital offers a compensation package that includes equity for all full-time employees and an annual performance bonus. Employees also receive a comprehensive benefits package that includes an employer-matched retirement plan, generously subsidized healthcare with 100% employer-paid dental, vision, telemedicine, and virtual mental health counseling, parental leave, and paid time off (PTO).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe the best ideas and innovation happen when we are together. Employees in this role will work in the office Monday-Thursday, with the flexibility to work remotely on Friday.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For additional information on iCapital, please visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.icapitalnetwork.com/about-us&quot;&gt;https://www.icapitalnetwork.com/about-us&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp; Twitter: @icapitalnetwork | LinkedIn: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/icapital-network-inc&quot;&gt;https://www.linkedin.com/company/icapital-network-inc&lt;/a&gt; | Awards Disclaimer: &lt;a href=&quot;https://nam02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.icapitalnetwork.com%2Fabout-us%2Frecognition%2F&amp;amp;data=05%7C01%7Ckturlis%40icapitalnetwork.com%7C7f07161790634b9fc3fc08da748bec16%7C0ac51d2823c34b35a9fbe1a17aa9eff1%7C0%7C0%7C637950441561507201%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;amp;sdata=HAZm4uhhP8r6HVKnBqOMq5jbXmgOrHlsPCur9U4JRis%3D&amp;amp;reserved=0&quot;&gt;https://www.icapitalnetwork.com/about-us/recognition/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;iCapital is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, or other applicable legally protected characteristics&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;iCapital is seeking a Senior Client Relationship Manager, Vice President.&amp;nbsp; This individual is responsible for leading sales coverage in Texas and Oklahoma based in Houston, Austin or Dallas/Fort Worth area. This role is part of iCapital’s Alternatives Distribution Sales team and will report to the Regional Director. The team is responsible for alternative investment product sales and financial advisor education across registered investment advisors, regional and independent broker dealers and bank trust clientele.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute a consultative sales process to increase adoption of alternatives with existing and new users and deliver world class service to existing platform asset holders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop sales proficiency across private credit, private equity, real estate, and hedge funds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help advisors build better portfolios, have better conversations, and build better businesses.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular in-market meetings with advisors, GP partners, and COIs to build trust and better understand market trends and opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in the alternative investment industry in a client facing capacity (e.g. external wholesaler, capital raising specialist, client portfolio manager, product specialist)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated, client first, adaptable, team player, with a desire to build a sales career with an industry leader&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in RIA, Independent BD or Bank distribution segments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success building a region, using data and CRM to inform decisions, and implementation of a well-defined sales process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to sell and provide post sale support for a world-class platform of hedge funds, private equity, private credit, and real estate offerings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Series 7 and 63 licenses are required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CAIA certified or obtain within three years of hire&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $150,000 to $175,000. iCapital offers a compensation package which includes salary and equity for all full-time employees. This role will include a commission based bonus. Employees also receive a comprehensive benefits package that includes an employer matched retirement plan, generously subsidized healthcare with 100% employer paid dental, vision, telemedicine, and virtual mental health counseling, parental leave, and unlimited paid time off (PTO).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employees in this role will work fully remote based in the Houston, Austin, or Dallas/Fort Worth area. Every department has different needs, and some positions will be designated in-office jobs, based on their function.&lt;/p&gt;
