&lt;p&gt;iCapital is looking to hire a Vice President to join the Structured Investments team. This role will support the Structured Investments team, within the firm’s technology platform, by owning, developing, and maintaining the structured investments eco-system on the platform for clients.&amp;nbsp; The team develops and manages the technology platform experience with many of iCapital’s largest clients, including investment banks, broker-dealers, private banks, and RIAs throughout the United States. This individual will help manage and grow relationships with our issuing partners, serving as a key point of contact and assisting in developing and executing the firm’s strategy and solutions in the structured investments market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the management of relationships with iCapital&#39;s issuing partners, serving as a key point of contact — coordinating regular touchpoints such as meetings, check-ins, and events, and responding to partner questions and requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help maintain and grow existing partnerships and support the onboarding of new issuers onto the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate partner needs and feedback into platform enhancements, owning the resulting projects and partnering with Product and Engineering to prioritize and deliver them while balancing competing partner priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop presentations, updates, and reporting for both partners and internal stakeholders, using data and analysis to inform decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aggregate, manipulate, and analyze large data sets to generate reports and surface insights, with excellent attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with teams across the firm — including Product, Engineering, Legal, Marketing, and Compliance — to deliver a robust, well-supported platform solution and drive process improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in the development and execution of the firm&#39;s overarching strategy for the Structured Investments business line.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant experience in trading, business development, or relationship management in the structured investments market or broader financial markets industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with or covering structured products is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills and a high level of attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to successfully operate in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic mindset and able to work independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated client service skills with stakeholders and clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desire to work in a cross-functional and collaborative environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Microsoft Suite (Excel, PowerPoint, Word)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Series 7 and 63 certifications are required or obtained within 90 days of hire&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $170,000 to $200,000.&amp;nbsp; iCapital offers a compensation package which includes salary, equity for all full-time employees, and an annual performance bonus. Employees also receive a comprehensive benefits package that includes an employer matched retirement plan, generously subsidized healthcare with 100% employer paid dental, vision, telemedicine, and virtual mental health counseling, parental leave, and unlimited paid time off (PTO).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe the best ideas and innovation happen when we are together. Employees in this role will work in the office Monday-Thursday, with the flexibility to work remotely on Friday.&lt;/p&gt;
