&lt;li&gt;Perform revenue calculations and controls for various product lines across iCapital, primarily Technology Solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure precision in monthly and quarterly revenue estimates and actuals, providing insightful analyses of variances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of financial excellence by collaborating with client relationship managers, finance leadership and external client contacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review legal agreements, contracts and other key documents and understand relevant economic terms as they relate to revenue and reporting and apply that understanding to revenue calculations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support full revenue cycle including order processing, invoicing, payment collection and revenue recognition, ensuring accuracy and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spearhead month-end close processes, preparing revenue calculations and revenue accruals for technology solutions products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calculate and consolidate P&amp;amp;L and balance sheet data, ensuring accurate journal entries for various entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the calculation and generation of invoices at month end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform month over month roll forwards for key revenue metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare detailed monthly revenue reconciliation analyses supporting accurate P&amp;amp;L reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute cash application processes and prepare monthly cash reconciliations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the initiative to enhance efficiency and automation of our existing revenue calculations and invoicing processes, including implementation of a new order-to-cash billing and receivable software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop insightful reporting and analyses to support business unit and product line leads with actionable insights for performance reporting to management and investors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and address process gaps, implement robust internal controls, and improve documentation for internal control processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to streamline processes by leveraging automation tools and data-driven workflows to improve efficiency and accelerate task completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-5 years of corporate accounting or public accounting experience within the financial services industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding financial analysis skills and knowledge of accounting principles and US GAAP&amp;nbsp;reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to apply critical thinking skills to analyze complex issues and propose effective solutions, while consistently maintaining a meticulous attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized and detail-oriented process manager who can prioritize and communicate clearly with senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with revenue, treasury management, accounts receivable and payable, and cash reconciliations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of booking journal entries and preparation of financial statements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven thinker who can manage large data sets for efficient analyses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with Microsoft Office Suite (Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to coordinate across teams and departments to complete projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPA license is preferred but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Accounting is preferred but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with Oracle NetSuite or other general ledger systems (i.e. Quickbooks) is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with alternative investments or structured investments is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
