&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;iCapital is looking to hire a Head of Canadian Legal to with a focus on Canadian funds and securities law issues as iCapital expands its offering in the region. The focus of this role will include representing iCapital in connection with Canadian private funds on a wide spectrum of matters including capital raising, marketing, investor relations, fund formation and structuring, corporate transactional matters, etc.&amp;nbsp; The role will also be responsible for helping develop iCapital’s Canadian entity governance structure, compliance, and regulatory issues, and expanding iCapital’s technology platform to be accessible to Canadian investors. This position will work closely with the General Counsel and International Legal Counsel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate various agreements with counterparties including fund managers and distribution agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft and review of private fund offering materials, partnership agreements, and other private fund legal documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as in-region expert on Canadian securities laws and regulatory concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on the legal implications of offering new and existing products and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with outside legal counsel with respect to a variety of issues including regulatory, corporate and fund investment work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft and review various contracts, non-disclosure agreements, and other legal documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform ad hoc research projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of fund formation experience within the Investment Management space in Canada (Private Equity and Hedge Fund)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of provincial and territorial securities laws, instruments, and policies; detailed knowledge and experience with registrant regulation (including NI 31-103 and IIROC), private placements and laws of general application to an asset management business and fund offerings in Canada (including privacy, money laundering and sanctions)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience in Canadian securities laws and regulatory framework, drafting and negotiating fund documents, side letters, placement agreements and related fund materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Member in good standing of the Law Society of Ontario or the equivalent in another province Law firm or in-house experience at an asset management firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal and leadership skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to learn new topics and work in an evolving business environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized and detail-oriented with big picture capability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with U.S. securities laws is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe the best ideas and innovation happen when we are together. Employees in this role will work in the office Monday-Thursday, with the flexibility to work remotely on Friday.&lt;/p&gt;
