&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;iCapital is seeking an experienced, strategic-thinking Dynamics Tech Lead to support the launch and scalability of Microsoft Dynamics 365 across the enterprise. This role is responsible for hands-on development, configuration, and support of Microsoft Dynamics applications, ensuring the smooth operation and integration of Dynamics solutions to meet evolving business needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead day-to-day development for Dynamics 365 Customer Service and Dataverse, partnering closely with the Architect, Product Owner, and QA Lead while contributing hands-on code alongside the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own code review standards and review changes across plug-ins, client scripts, Power Automate flows, and solution components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define engineering practices for solution layering, source control, branching, environment management, coding standards, templates, and reusable development patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own CI/CD pipelines in Azure DevOps, enabling repeatable and governed releases from development through production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver enhancements across case management, SLAs, queues, routing, security roles, and other core Dynamics 365 Customer Service capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement Dynamics 365 Contact Center capabilities, including channel configuration and unified routing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build Copilot Studio agents and Copilot features for service agents and customers, incorporating effective grounding, hand-off, and guardrail design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build enterprise integrations with platforms such as ServiceNow, Pega, and Salesforce using APIs, Dataverse, and Power Automate, with appropriate error handling and monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Launch secure customer self-service capabilities, including a portal with authentication, role-based access, and data protection suited to a regulated business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver a customer-facing chatbot integrated with the self-service portal, case management capabilities, and live agent hand-off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take technical ownership of the platform, including the technical backlog, codebase, solutions, and documentation, as part of the transition from the implementation partner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor developers, establish scalable engineering practices, and help shape the in-house engineering function, including proposing additional development hiring as demand grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive hands-on development experience with Microsoft Dynamics 365 Customer Service, Dataverse, and the Power Platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in C#, JavaScript, and TypeScript, including experience developing plug-ins, custom APIs, and client-side scripts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading developers, conducting code reviews, mentoring team members, and establishing engineering standards for business-critical applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building enterprise integrations using REST APIs, including exposure to platforms such as ServiceNow, Pega, or Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Power Automate and CI/CD for Power Platform solutions, including experience with Azure DevOps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of security roles, authentication, secure access patterns, and data protection requirements for portals and external users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing conversational AI solutions, including Copilot Studio agents or comparable technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Dynamics 365 Contact Center or Omnichannel for Customer Service, including contact center capabilities and routing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering customer self-service solutions, including Power Pages or other portals and customer-facing chatbots&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with Azure services, including Functions, Service Bus, API Management, and Microsoft Entra ID&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting enterprise platforms in financial services or another regulated industry, including experience transitioning a platform from an implementation partner and building in-house development capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to explain technical decisions and trade-offs to both technical and business audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Microsoft certifications preferred, including Microsoft Certified: Dynamics 365 Customer Service Functional Consultant Associate (MB-230), Dynamics 365 Contact Center AI Engineer Associate (AB-250), Power Platform Developer Associate (AB-400), or Power Platform Solution Architect (PL-600)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $120,000 to $160,000.&amp;nbsp; iCapital offers a compensation package which includes salary, equity for all full-time employees, and an annual performance bonus. Employees also receive a comprehensive benefits package that includes an employer matched retirement plan, generously subsidized healthcare with 100% employer paid dental, vision, telemedicine, and virtual mental health counseling, parental leave, and unlimited paid time off (PTO).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
