&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product Owners, architects, and the QA, DevOps, Support and client-facing teams to define requirements, resolve dependencies and deliver end-to-end solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure high standards of code quality, security, performance, reliability, testability and maintainability through code reviews, testing, root-cause analysis and engineering best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and resolve complex issues across applications, APIs, databases, configurations, deployments and external system integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive reusable integration patterns, common services, monitoring, logging, error-handling strategies and continuous improvement initiatives that improve platform scalability and operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical leadership through design reviews, architectural discussions, mentoring, knowledge sharing and guidance to engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Agile delivery activities, including estimation, sprint planning, release management, CI/CD processes and production readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify design, quality, delivery and operational risks proactively. Communicate technical solutions, risks, dependencies and recommendations to technical and nontechnical stakeholders while balancing customer needs with long-term platform sustainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide occasional off-hours or weekend support for critical production issues, deployments and business-critical activities, as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of software development experience delivering testable code and supporting operationalization as needed, with expertise in code reviews, configurability, source-code management, release practices and production support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of hands-on software development experience using C#, .NET and ASP.NET MVC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in C# and .NET, including object-oriented programming, application services, controllers, models, asynchronous programming and common .NET engineering practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong self-starter with exceptional verbal and written communication skills, able to engage directly with clients, understand business needs, and translate them into effective technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of SOLID principles, common design patterns, modular development, microservice architecture and reusable software design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced experience designing and consuming REST APIs, including authentication, authorization, validation, versioning, security and resilient error handling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with XML, JSON, Entity Framework, LINQ, SQL and Postman for enterprise integration development and troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid experience with Git and Azure DevOps, including repositories, builds, CI/CD pipelines, releases, deployments and work-item management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong debugging and root-cause analysis skills across logs, APIs, payloads, databases, configuration, application code, pipelines and deployment behavior&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with NUnit, xUnit or MSTest, and a strong understanding of test coverage and testable design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of application security, sensitive-data handling, logging, monitoring, reliability and configuration-management principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work occasional off-hours or weekend support as needed&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in an Agile and Scrum team environment; Scrum Master experience &lt;em&gt;is preferred&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of HTML, CSS and JavaScript for supporting end-to-end functionality; professional experience with React is &lt;em&gt;nice to have&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success leading technical delivery, mentoring engineers, influencing solution quality and communicating complex topics to technical and nontechnical stakeholders is &lt;em&gt;strongly preferred&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $110,000 to $130,000 USD.&amp;nbsp; iCapital offers a compensation package which includes salary, equity for all full-time employees, and an annual performance bonus. Employees also receive a comprehensive benefits package that includes an employer matched retirement plan, generously subsidized healthcare with 100% employer paid dental, vision, telemedicine, and virtual mental health counseling, parental leave, and unlimited paid time off (PTO).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe the best ideas and innovation happen when we are together. Employees in this role will work in the office Monday-Thursday, with the flexibility to work remotely on Friday.&amp;nbsp; This role is based in our Salt Lake City office.&lt;/p&gt;
