&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;iCapital is looking to hire a Vice President, Strategic Accounts to drive new business growth and develop long-term strategic relationships across the life insurance and annuity market. This individual will own the full client lifecycle and serves as both a strategic seller and trusted advisor, developing a deep understanding of clients’ businesses, priorities, and growth objectives and aligning iCapital’s solutions to support their success. This individual will work independently to develop and execute account strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate sustainable revenue and take responsibility for achieving and exceeding assigned sales and growth targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, develop, and close new business opportunities while maintaining a healthy and well-managed sales pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own client relationships across the full commercial lifecycle, from prospecting and opportunity development through ongoing relationship management, retention, and expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of prospective and existing clients’ businesses, strategic goals, priorities, challenges, and growth initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain trusted relationships with executive, business, technology, and operational stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute strategic account plans that address client objectives, revenue opportunities, relationship priorities, and retention risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present and demonstrate iCapital products and services, connecting capabilities to client needs and strategic objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular business reviews, strategic planning sessions, and account health assessments with key clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify expansion opportunities, account risks, and client needs and develop appropriate action plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the voice of the customer internally and partner with Product, Client Delivery, Production Support, and Leadership to address client needs and execute strategic initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the resolution of escalated client issues through proactive communication, stakeholder alignment, and consistent follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a deep understanding of iCapital’s platform, products, processes, capabilities, and product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay informed of life insurance, annuity, distribution, technology, and broader industry trends and incorporate relevant insights into client strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate Salesforce records, account plans, opportunities, forecasts, client activity, and other required documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in industry events, conferences, working groups, and associations to develop relationships, identify opportunities, and strengthen iCapital’s industry presence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8-10+ years of experience across enterprise sales, strategic account management, relationship management, customer success, consulting, or similar client-facing roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of insurance industry experience, with strong knowledge of life insurance, annuity products, carrier operations, and insurance distribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success selling complex SaaS, technology, or enterprise solutions and managing sophisticated client relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successful track record of achieving or exceeding revenue, sales, retention, or growth objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing the full client lifecycle, including prospecting, complex sales processes, relationship management, retention, and expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with insurance carriers, distributors, IMOs, BGAs, or other life and annuity market participants is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build relationships with senior and executive-level stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic planning, consultative selling, presentation, negotiation, communication, and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to influence outcomes across multiple departments and stakeholders without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with sales qualification methodologies such as MEDDPICC and knowledge of Mutual Action Plans is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and Salesforce.com or comparable CRM platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to travel up to 50% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $125,000 to $135,000. iCapital offers a compensation package which includes salary, equity for all full-time employees, and an annual performance bonus. Employees also receive a comprehensive benefits package that includes an employer matched retirement plan, generously subsidized healthcare with 100% employer paid dental, vision, telemedicine, and virtual mental health counseling, parental leave, and unlimited paid time off (PTO).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employees in this role will work fully remote. Every department has different needs, and some positions will be designated in-office jobs, based on their function.&lt;/p&gt;
