&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;iCapital is looking to hire an Analyst to join the Structured Investments team to focus on sales support. This position will work cross-functionally and closely with bank issuers and clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct calls to set appointments for licensed sales professionals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn iCapital products and prepare to effectively communicate the objectives, risks, features, and benefits of these products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze regional and product sales trends within participating broker-dealer firms and among individual Financial Advisors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make 50+ outbound calls per day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn financial markets and portfolio strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist senior sales professionals within assigned territory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively partner with the external wholesaler and the regional distribution team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize contact management systems to capture information and schedule follow up activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare for and pass necessary licenses.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree is required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0-2 years of relevant experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sales and client service experience, within the financial services industry is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent relationship, follow-up, and communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;General knowledge of the financial services industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivated, mature, trustworthy, and a team player&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized and able to prioritize in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of private markets, structured products, and options is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Series 7, 63 and SIE (FINRA) licenses or candidate must obtain licenses within 4 months of hire date&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
