&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;iCapital is seeking a Technology Program Manager to partner closely with Engineering and Technology leadership teams to deliver complex, high-impact initiatives across the firm’s most critical technology priorities. This role sits at the intersection of strategy and execution, bringing best-in-class program management practices to large-scale, cross-functional initiatives. The team operates in an internal consulting capacity, driving clarity, alignment, and disciplined execution across multi-team programs. This individual will engage across a diverse portfolio including greenfield software development, enterprise vendor implementations, cloud and infrastructure initiatives, data and analytics and machine learning efforts, and broader technology innovation programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;As iCapital continues to scale, the company is increasingly leveraging AI-enabled tools and automation to enhance engineering productivity and program transparency. This role requires comfort operating in an AI-augmented environment, identifying opportunities to use emerging technologies to improve planning, reporting, decision-making, and cross-team coordination. This is a leadership and execution role focused on orchestration, visibility, and delivery excellence; it does not involve hands-on coding or testing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end delivery of complex, cross-functional technology programs spanning multiple engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Engineering teams to define scope, roadmap, milestones, and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear governance, reporting, and risk management practices to ensure transparency and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate program status, risks, dependencies, and mitigation strategies to senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Technology leadership to shape forward-looking strategy and execution frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement initiatives to enhance delivery effectiveness across the broader Technology teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring structure and clarity to ambiguous or evolving initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-10 years of relevant experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in engineering, computer science, business administration, or related field preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in at least two of the following: technical program management, financial services industry, or technology or financial services consulting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of software development lifecycle (SDLC) methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with relational database concepts and data modeling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to cloud technologies (i.e. AWS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with project management tools such as JIRA, Monday.com, or similar platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to influence stakeholders and build consensus across diverse viewpoints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinker who can connect big-picture objectives to detailed execution plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable navigating complexity and ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional verbal and written communication skills and organizational skills with attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal skills with a collaborative, team-oriented mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to operate effectively both independently and within cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PMP certification is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $100,000 to $120,000.&amp;nbsp; iCapital offers a compensation package which includes salary, equity for all full-time employees, and an annual performance bonus. Employees also receive a comprehensive benefits package that includes an employer matched retirement plan, generously subsidized healthcare with 100% employer paid dental, vision, telemedicine, and virtual mental health counseling, parental leave, and unlimited paid time off (PTO).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe the best ideas and innovation happen when we are together. Employees in this role will work in the office Monday-Thursday, with the flexibility to work remotely on Friday.&lt;/p&gt;
