&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;iCapital is looking to hire a Production Support Analyst (PSA) to provide front-line technical support for iCapital&#39;s annuities eApplication platform, ensuring timely resolution of client inquiries and system-related issues. This role serves as a critical point of contact for clients, delivering exceptional service while troubleshooting technical challenges, escalating critical incidents, and collaborating across teams to maintain platform performance. The PSA plays a key role in driving client satisfaction, improving operational efficiency, and contributing to continuous process enhancements through knowledge sharing and workflow development. This position supports clients during the 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM EST shift and operates under general supervision within a collaborative, fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Production Support team members to maintain active engagement during working hours and share workload responsibilities equitably.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to client inquiries and support requests with urgency, professionalism, and a focus on timely resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify critical issues and coordinate with cross-functional iCapital teams to drive prompt escalation and resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain or exceed established response-time compliance standards and service level expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver high-quality client experience to maintain or exceed customer satisfaction targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and contribute to standardized workflows, best practices, and process improvement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform technical support and ticket resolution activities under general supervision while demonstrating sound judgment and accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-3 years’ experience in technology industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience providing direct end user support for software (either custom built software or SAAS model platform)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with online ticketing system and support; experience with Jira is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating user documentation; experience with Jira Confluence and SharePoint is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in insurance industry is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is $60,000 to $75,000. This position is paid on an hourly basis and is classified as non-exempt. Employees in this role are eligible for overtime pay in accordance with applicable law. iCapital offers a compensation package that includes equity for all full-time employees and an annual performance bonus. Employees also receive a comprehensive benefits package that includes an employer-matched retirement plan, generously subsidized healthcare with 100% employer-paid dental, vision, telemedicine, and virtual mental health counseling, parental leave, and paid time off (PTO).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe the best ideas and innovation happen when we are together. Employees in this role will work in the office Monday-Thursday, with the flexibility to work remotely on Friday.&amp;nbsp; This position can be based in the greater Colorado Springs, CO area, or the greater Des Moines, IA area.&lt;/p&gt;
